First measurement under the frame ratified after INV-duvup. NOT comparable to
0001/0004/0005; the series restarts here.

112 situations, 16 repositories, 10 languages, seed 20260825.
Situation 38/112 = 33.9%; row 106/336 = 31.5%; UNADJ 0.

The frame worked: largest single repository contributes 14.6% of rows, against
77% / 75% / 50% in earlier cohorts. A per-repository precision spread of
0%-85.7% that concentration had hidden is now visible.

Protocol (F7, four passes). Both labelling passes were independent agent
panels and the orchestrator held none -- a deviation from 0005, recorded in
PANEL-DESIGN-NOTE.md rather than glossed, because panel A was launched before
the orchestrator's pass existed and agents return labels into its context.
Agreement 94.6%; pass 3 adjudicated the 6 splits; pass 4 refuted 7 of 44 TPs
(15.9%) against 0005's 1 of 9.

Two sensitivities were pre-registered with their arithmetic and withheld from
the refuters. The larger fired exactly as priced (39.3% -> 36.6%); three
further refutations landed outside both.

One refutation (tmux#6) is reported separately and NOT folded in: it rests on
an anchor criterion absent from 0001's rubric that the adjudicator introduced
in the refutation brief. F6 forbids rewriting the cited rubric mid-measurement.

Dominant incidental defect family: a primitive classified by NAME rather than
by what it does, across five languages. A finding can be true value-flow and
vacuous as a claim, which makes 33.9% an upper bound on useful precision.

